; TYPE prints like PRINT, but without a trailing newline -- several
; TYPEs (or a TYPE followed by a PRINT) build up one line piece by piece.

TYPE "Hello,
TYPE "
PRINT "world!

; SHOW prints a user-defined procedure's own TO ... END definition back
; out, exactly as SAVE would write it to a file.

TO square :size
  REPEAT 4 [FD :size RT 90]
END
SHOW "square

; An undefined procedure name reports an error instead of a crash.

SHOW "nope
